//==
// # BrepCheckingWhere
//
// Layer 7 of the STEP B-rep to mesh design (README.md beside this file): one
// Check_ per WHERE rule law of 03-step (step-where.laws.plato), each the law
// evaluated at every instance position of a Part21File and reported at the
// instance's name; every law guards its own entity kind, so it is vacuous at
// the other positions. The two laws that take an AngleTolerance are evaluated
// with the decode policy's AngleCoincidence, the tolerance the decoder itself
// uses. A WHERE rule is an exact statement about the file (structure): a
// failure is an Error, except the four that layer 3 grades lower, named in
// their comments: three are reported as Warnings (WarningReport) and one as
// Info (QualityReport). WhereRulesReport
// merges them all. The checks were generated from the law signatures of
// step-where.laws.plato, one per law, so no name is retyped by hand.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Units
//  - Points, directions, placements
//  - Curves
//  - Curves on surfaces
//  - Surfaces
//  - Topology
//  - Advanced faces
//  - Representations and placement links
//  - The report of every WHERE rule

library BrepCheckingWhere
{
    //==
    // # Units

    // Law_Where_UncertaintyMeasureWithUnit_WR1 at every instance position.
    // Structure: Error.
    Check_Where_UncertaintyMeasureWithUnit_WR1(f: Part21File): Check
        => f.CheckInstances("Law_Where_UncertaintyMeasureWithUnit_WR1", i => Law_Where_UncertaintyMeasureWithUnit_WR1(f, i));

    // Law_Where_LengthMeasureWithUnit_WR1 at every instance position.
